# ES5 in js/

cha.mdc is authoritative here. This file adds detail it does not
enumerate.

Async work uses .then().catch() as cha.mdc specifies. async/await is
forbidden.

Also forbidden, beyond the list in cha.mdc: class, destructuring, default
parameters, spread and rest, for...of, Object.assign,
Array.prototype.includes, Array.prototype.find,
String.prototype.startsWith, Object.entries, Object.values.

Use instead: var, function expressions, string concatenation, indexOf, a
plain for loop.

These files ship to the browser with no transpile step. Modern syntax
does not fail loudly here. It fails on one agent's older browser in the
middle of a live call.

## Defensive habits

- Guard every DOM lookup. getElementById returns null on tabs where the
  element is not rendered, and this app renders several.
- Toggle an existing class rather than writing element.style directly
  when a class for that state already exists.

## Before adding a helper

Search js/ for an existing one. This codebase already has utilities for
most common operations, and several are frozen. Duplicating one is how
the two copies drift apart.
